:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T17:33:14-07:00","id":178447,"title":"","content":"&quot;Look, if you can't deal with a little bit of viscera in the common area maybe a communal living arrangement isn't for you&quot;<br /> <br /> Y'all, if I joke about this any more I'm actually going to have to play this character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T18:07:52-07:00","id":178469,"title":"","content":"*Irraka comes into the common area* <br /> <br /> Livers! I love livers!<br /> <br /> *starts to munch on them.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T19:35:36-07:00","id":178538,"title":"","content":"&quot;Okay, that's still a little too gross for me, I'm out&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That's not what you said last night&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;YOU TRY SPEAKING COHERENTLY IN GAURU!&quot;<br /> <br /> We're totally playing this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T19:41:25-07:00","id":178545,"title":"","content":"A liver is tossed to the loud mouth, square on the chest.<br /> <br /> Viscera chin stained Irraka looked like a dog who had taken a shit on the kitchen.<br /> <br /> &quot;I thought you were hungry.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T20:31:58-07:00","id":178589,"title":"","content":"Seriously, when Idigam comes out, we're taking this pack and playing it in the forums/chats. I even know who my girl is.<br /> <br /> PS: At this point I'm fairly sure her response is probably to go wreck your car or to start hitting you, I don't think we want die rolls at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-24-2014, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T03:09:23-07:00","id":178766,"title":"","content":"Because I'm feeling silly and indulgent this morning, a Pack Rite:<br /> <br /> <b>Feast of the Liver (ooo)</b><br /> This rite draws on ancient pacts that bind spirits of greed, gluttony, dominance and cannibalism.<br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Viscera, greed, dominance, fortune<br /> <b>Target:</b> 10 successes (1 roll = 5 minutes)<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The rite requires the liver of a human that the pack has killed while they were the target of the Siskur-Dah. The ritual bestows up to two dots of Merits that the victim possessed on a single pack member. This <i>can </i>bestow supernatural Merits, but this doubles the number of successes required for the rite. As part of the rite, the target is given a piece of the liver that they must keep about their person; the rite's benefit immediately terminates if the character no longer possesses the liver piece. Some practices have the liver piece dried or preserved, others insist that the blessing only be kept as long as the chunk of offal remains bloody. Commonly, the liver piece is kept in a small bag or other container, like a gris-gris bag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T03:13:58-07:00","id":178768,"title":"","content":"This feels like the cast of Friends as a pack of Uratha.<br /> <br /> ...which I would <i><b>totally</b> play</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'll be there for you<br /> When the moon starts to call...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T05:54:14-07:00","id":178844,"title":"","content":"The Elodoth looks up from the dog-eared copy of some book he found, rolls his eyes,and shifts a quarter-turn away to protect his acquisition from the splatter of an inevitable liver-fight.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'll be there for you<br /> When you need some <i>Ulal</i>....&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T08:25:59-07:00","id":178949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175563-no-forsaken-friday-this-week?p=178766#post178766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I'm feeling silly and indulgent this morning, a Pack Rite:<br /> <br /> <b>Feast of the Liver (ooo)</b><br /> This rite draws on ancient pacts that bind spirits of greed, gluttony, dominance and cannibalism.<br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Viscera, greed, dominance, fortune<br /> <b>Target:</b> 10 successes (1 roll = 5 minutes)<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The rite requires the liver of a human that the pack has killed while they were the target of the Siskur-Dah. The ritual bestows two of Merits that the victim possessed on a single pack member<b>, at the rating that the victim possessed them</b>. This <i>can </i>bestow supernatural Merits, but this doubles the number of successes required for the rite. As part of the rite, the target is given a piece of the liver that they must keep about their person; the rite's benefit immediately terminates if the character no longer possesses the liver piece. Some practices have the liver piece dried or preserved, others insist that the blessing only be kept as long as the chunk of offal remains bloody. Commonly, the liver piece is kept in a small bag or other container, like a gris-gris bag. <b>Or eaten. At which point the effect last a whole lunar month. Participants who do this face a breaking point towards spirit.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Added stuff. Most supernatural merits are at least 3 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 06-24-2014, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T11:05:26-07:00","id":179073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175563-no-forsaken-friday-this-week?p=178766#post178766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I'm feeling silly and indulgent this morning, a Pack Rite:<br /> <br /> <b>Feast of the Liver (ooo)</b><br /> This rite draws on ancient pacts that bind spirits of greed, gluttony, dominance and cannibalism.<br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Viscera, greed, dominance, fortune<br /> <b>Target:</b> 10 successes (1 roll = 5 minutes)<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The rite requires the liver of a human that the pack has killed while they were the target of the Siskur-Dah. The ritual bestows up to two dots of Merits that the victim possessed on a single pack member. This <i>can </i>bestow supernatural Merits, but this doubles the number of successes required for the rite. As part of the rite, the target is given a piece of the liver that they must keep about their person; the rite's benefit immediately terminates if the character no longer possesses the liver piece. Some practices have the liver piece dried or preserved, others insist that the blessing only be kept as long as the chunk of offal remains bloody. Commonly, the liver piece is kept in a small bag or other container, like a gris-gris bag.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that you can pump out a quick, joke Merit that is nevertheless <i>something I'd totally take</i> speaks volumes, man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T13:26:51-07:00","id":179195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175563-no-forsaken-friday-this-week?p=179073#post179073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that you can pump out a quick, joke Merit that is nevertheless <i>something I'd totally take</i> speaks volumes, man.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rite, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T15:13:29-07:00","id":179269,"title":"","content":"Heh. Eat a liver, get the Barfly merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T19:39:25-07:00","id":179418,"title":"","content":"::wipes gore off mouth::<br /> <br /> Now I'm classy and everyone wants me at their parties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T19:48:31-07:00","id":179421,"title":"","content":"I'd do that.<br /> <br /> &quot;...yeah, me too.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T22:46:29-07:00","id":179483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175563-no-forsaken-friday-this-week?p=179269#post179269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh. Eat a liver, get the Barfly merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Striking Looks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T02:43:19-07:00","id":179553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175563-no-forsaken-friday-this-week?p=179483#post179483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Striking Looks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;That's a hell of a lipstick shade!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T06:03:58-07:00","id":179611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175563-no-forsaken-friday-this-week?p=179195#post179195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rite, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Rite. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Would you say that the ritualist should only be able to select Merits that they could plausibly know the victim had, or should the Storyteller give the ritualist a list of selectable Merits?<br /> <br /> Also, I liked Ephsy's changes, but it begs the question if one can have multiple effects up at once, or hold multiple pieces of liver from different instances of the rite. Obviously it's not easy to exploit or abuse this, since it requires a new Siskur-Dah per target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T11:33:02-07:00","id":179885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175563-no-forsaken-friday-this-week?p=178949#post178949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>, at the rating that the victim possessed them</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I pondered that and decided not to worry about it. If you have a moderately wealthy pack member who you want to be richer, you don't need to go eat a millionaire's liver for it. Go murder another hapless moderately wealthy person and wallow in the gorey fortune that your pack promptly amasses.<br /> <br /> i.e. If the subject has Resources 2 and the victim has Resources 2, chop chop and your pack-mate now has Resources 4.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <b>Or eaten. At which point the effect last a whole lunar month. Participants who do this face a breaking point towards spirit.</b><br /> <br /> Added stuff. Most supernatural merits are at least 3 dots. </div> </div> </div>I pondered the eating side of it, but I'm torn; I like my ritualists to be decked out in weird fetishes and talens, trinkets, charms, bags, wards and the like, so my preference runs more towards the rite having a focus that can be lost or stolen. That said, there's a strong thematic reason to have the eating element in there, I just reckon that a breaking point towards Spirit is a fairly weak downside for removing the vulnerability of the physical focus. Maybe you have to do both; consume part of the liver and keep another part in a bag or container on you. Hmm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175563-no-forsaken-friday-this-week?p=179611#post179611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, Rite. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Would you say that the ritualist should only be able to select Merits that they could plausibly know the victim had, or should the Storyteller give the ritualist a list of selectable Merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would very much advise the ritemaster make damn sure he or she knows a viable Merit that the victim has. This shouldn't give a shopping list of Merits, you should be targeting a victim with the Hunt because you intend to make pate out of their liver to get Resources, or Allies, or Striking Looks, or whatever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I liked Ephsy's changes, but it begs the question if one can have multiple effects up at once, or hold multiple pieces of liver from different instances of the rite. Obviously it's not easy to exploit or abuse this, since it requires a new Siskur-Dah per target. </div> </div> </div>Doh, I forgot about duration and the stacking restrictions. Assume it lasts for one season (or maybe just one lunar month, depends how harsh I feel, not sure at the moment <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) and you can only benefit from one Feast of the Liver at one time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T11:39:23-07:00","id":179887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe you have to do both; consume part of the liver and keep another part in a bag or container on you. Hmm. </div> </div> </div>Yes, this, I like this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T12:33:24-07:00","id":179945,"title":"","content":"Until you hit a human breaking point? Seems like something that could be taken advantage of, while also solidifying the link to the spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T15:40:15-07:00","id":180126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175563-no-forsaken-friday-this-week?p=179885#post179885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I pondered the eating side of it, but I'm torn; I like my ritualists to be decked out in weird fetishes and talens, trinkets, charms, bags, wards and the like, so my preference runs more towards the rite having a focus that can be lost or stolen. That said, there's a strong thematic reason to have the eating element in there, I just reckon that a breaking point towards Spirit is a fairly weak downside for removing the vulnerability of the physical focus. Maybe you have to do both; consume part of the liver and keep another part in a bag or container on you. Hmm.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine cannibalism carries with their own possible Addiction Condition. Or Ban, but I dunno how that one works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T04:03:11-07:00","id":181817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/175563-no-forsaken-friday-this-week?p=178766#post178766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I'm feeling silly and indulgent this morning, a Pack Rite:<br /> <br /> <b>Feast of the Liver (ooo)</b><br /> This rite draws on ancient pacts that bind spirits of greed, gluttony, dominance and cannibalism.<br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Viscera, greed, dominance, fortune<br /> <b>Target:</b> 10 successes (1 roll = 5 minutes)<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The rite requires the liver of a human that the pack has killed while they were the target of the Siskur-Dah. The ritual bestows up to two dots of Merits that the victim possessed on a single pack member. This <i>can </i>bestow supernatural Merits, but this doubles the number of successes required for the rite. As part of the rite, the target is given a piece of the liver that they must keep about their person; the rite's benefit immediately terminates if the character no longer possesses the liver piece. Some practices have the liver piece dried or preserved, others insist that the blessing only be kept as long as the chunk of offal remains bloody. Commonly, the liver piece is kept in a small bag or other container, like a gris-gris bag.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well. Looks like something awesome for the Lodge of the Wendigo!<br /> And I don't care if it's a joke, it's a cool Rite!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}